-1 PKILL 'PKILL RULES'~
{110}                       --- Player Killing Rules ---
{120}Assassination:
{160}  Assistance from any other character is prohibited.  

{120}Hunting Assassins:
{160}  Assistance from other characters is allowed.  The only restrictions
  are the hard coded level restrictions.

{120}Clan Wars:
{160}  Only assistance from other members of your clan's army is allowed.
  Other "neutral" interaction is prohibited.

{120}Race Wars:
{160}  Only assistance from other members of your race's army is allowed.
  Other "neutral" interaction is prohibited.

{120}God Wars:
{160}  Only assistance from other followers of your god is allowed.  Other
  "neutral" interaction is prohibited.

{120}** A "neutral" character {160}is defined as a character who is NOT an active
   participant in the pkill venue in question.  (i.e.  A non-follower
   can not help a follower in any way.  A non-clanarmy character can 
   not help a clan army character.  And so on...)

{120}** The ONLY exceptions to these rules are:
{160}  - Using utilities to spell up the pkill characters
  - Using a spy to gather information on targets

{130}   (-) Back to Rules of the Realm{300}

{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD2 MULTIPLAY LIMIT~
Multi-Playing:
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Multi-Playing is defined as one person having more than one character
logged into the game at a time.  The current limit is FIVE characters
MAXIMUM at any one time.  During heavy periods of lag an admin will
notify players of a new limit.  The current limit for God followers
is ONE character at a time.  Violation of this rule is justification
for severe punishment.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD3~
Player Names:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Suitable names are an essential part of maintaining a role-playing 
environment.  Stupid names, names which involve profanity, or sexual 
implications, or names that use illegal words will NOT be tolerated.

eg: Double Words:  Blacklance, Lostgirl, Darkwarrior
eg: Stupid names:  Buttmunch, Dorkone, Dorktwo, Tdork, BGut, FFFunnyyy
eg: Illegal words: Lord, Lady, Sir, Miss, Maiden, Squire, Thee
eg: Handles:       TheBigOne, LordHolio, SirNerd, FrogBoy
eg: Similar names: Rhapsody and Rhapsodys

Names from contemporary television programs and movies are illegal.
We recognize that several current players have what would be considered
illegal names under the new rules.  So this policy kicks in: 16-Nov-95.
All players created before this date are considered exempt.  If you delete
a character with an illegal name, that name is no longer exempt.

Punishment for breaking this rule is immediate dungeoning until the character
auto-deletes or is renamed by a high level admin. There will be no level limit 
at which punishment will be waived.  If you want the equipment from the 
dungeoned character, post a note to the officers, after removing the equipment 
you must delete said character.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD4~
Harassment:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Harassment is defined as one person going to extremes to make the game
an unenjoyable place for another player.  What is "extreme" will be defined
by the admin for each specific situation. 

Player-killing, assassination, and steal are skills that can only be exercised 
in a limited fashion. Name-calling, swearing, unwanted sexual overtures etc are 
all forms of harassment that will not be tolerated.

Anything you communicate on any channel (notes, talk, chat, say, tell) about
someone else that is demeaning, degrading, or meant to humiliate may be
considered harassment.  For example: The skill 'spy' was meant specifically
as a help for assassination. What you overhear and tell to others by means of
spy can be considered harassment.

  (-) Back


{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD5~      
Bug Abuse:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bugs are defined as quirks in the coding that allow you to do things that
aren't intended as a part of game play.  This includes, but is not limited
to, loading multiple mobiles in a room, abusing mob or object programs to
load equipment, utilizing game code quirks to gain an advantage, such as
speed, improper group formation, and so on.  Using a bug in any way is 
considered abuse.  If you find a bug, report it IMMEDIATELY, so that it can
be taken care of.  Failure to report a bug or the use of a bug even after it
is reported is a severe offense and will get your character deleted!

Joking or chatting about bug abuse will be assumed to be factual, and will
carry the same action as witnessing the abuse in person.  Diversions or
"smoke screens" will not be tolerated, nor will they be rifled through to
determine their validity.

The abuse of bugs, or "game quirks", is not up for interpretation.  Those
who choose  to abuse such things are well aware of their actions as well
as their eventual fate.  If there is _any_ question as to the validity of
a feature in the game, it would be very wise to ask before using it.

Punishment for bug abuse is DELETION.


  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD6~
Scripts and Triggers:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game activity while away from your computer is not allowed.  Any activity
that benefits your characters in any way that is not attended will be
considered AFK activity and will be jailed accordingly.  Extenuating
circumstances such as attempts to cover up such activity may result in
longer sentences to be determined by the admin.


Scripting clients and triggers are allowed.  However, using scripts or
triggers to autolevel any character is illegal.  Movement of the character
(including fleeing and recalling) and the initiation of fights with 
mobiles MUST be performed manually by the player.  An admin may choose, 
but is not required, to test for the use of leveling scripts or triggers 
in many different fashions.

Punishment for scripting is AUTOMATIC DELETION, no questions asked.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD7~
Profanity and Inappropriate Language (Any Visible Information):
----------------------------------------------------------------------
We want all visible information that can be seen by everyone in the 
game to be as clean as possible.  No sexual implications, profanity, 
racist remarks, etc. will be tolerated in titles, tactical indexes, 
disguises, descriptions, email addresses, or any other form of 
written communication.

Punishment for inappropriate language will be determined by the
particular admin according to the magnitude of the offense.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD8~
Punishment:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Admins are expected to listen to your side of the story before any 
punishment, except for bug abuse and scripting.  If you choose to be rude
or have a bad attitude, the admin may slay, slaughter or execute you.

  SLAY       - Kills your character without loss of experience.
  SLAUGHTER  - Kills your character with loss of experience.
  DISCONNECT - Makes your character lose link.

Other options of punishment are:

  FREEZE       - Prevents you performing any commands.
  SILENCE      - Prevents you from speaking.
  SACRIFICE    - The ordered sacrificing of all your character's possessions.
  IMPRISONMENT - Keeps your character from doing anything productive for an
                 indefinite time.
  DELETION     - Deletion of character.
  DENIAL       - Prevent future attempts to login.

  NOTE: These jail terms for punishments are recommendations for jail
        sentences. The actual jail time is at the discretion of the
        jailer and may vary accordingly.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~
-1 MRPD9~
Sharing Characters:
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sharing characters is not authorized.  This means that any trouble caused
by a character, even if it's not being used by the player who created it,
will be paid for by the character.  Any disputes over ownership of a
shared character will be settled by the players.  Asking for help from a
god or officer to get a lost character back will not work.  The only way
to ensure your characters are protected is to use good passwords and trust
them to none other than yourself.  If you are going to share your character
with someone else, please make sure you do not give out the password on
the game.  Email or a phone call will protect you from having your password
spied upon.

The ONLY exception to this rule is in the case of a 1998 player file.
Possession of passwords for such characters does not constitute ownership
in this case.  This type of situation is subject to review by the admin, 
and can result in the character being locked from use.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~

-1 MRPDA1~
Spamming:
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Spamming is flooding another player with useless or irrelevant text. It is
typically done by repeating a command numerous times.  This is illegal.
It is legal to spam yourself if you think you are being spied upon.

The limits of spamming are as follows:
Any public channel (talk, chat, notes, etc.):  5 times.
Any private channel (tells, says): 10 times.
For player-killers who spam tintin users the limit is 15 times per
kill attempt. Note that is 15 times all together, not 15 times for
each tintin command.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~

-1 MRPD11~
Other:
------------------------------------------------------------------------
There are a few other rules to be aware of.

MUD MEETING ETIQUETTE - It is illegal to attack/assassinate/murder someone
who is in the process of leaving the room where a town meeting or Mud
meeting conducted by MR administrators is being held.

PKILLING LINKDEAD PLAYERS - It is illegal to attack a player that is
linklost/linkdead - even if you believe that the link was severed in order
to purposefully avoid death.

The punishments for these crimes are at the discretion of the
administrator.

  (-) Back



{-}MRPD1
~


-1 MRPD0 'PKILL SUMMON'~
Player Killing (What's legal and illegal?):
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Summoning an assassin with a killer flag to a guard                      LEGAL
Summoning an assassin with a killer flag to be murdered                  LEGAL
Summoning an opposite follower to be murdered by you                     LEGAL
Summoning an opp fol to be attacked by a fol of the same god as you      LEGAL
Summoning an army opp with an army char to be 'murdered' or 'battled'    LEGAL

Using a neutral character to assist in assassination (Except spying)   ILLEGAL
Summoning a follower or army with a neutral (Except when asked)        ILLEGAL
Summoning anyone to an aggressive mob                                  ILLEGAL
Summoning a player to be assassinated                                  ILLEGAL

 NOTE: Guards only attack killers and thieves.  They are not aggressive mobs.
 NOTE: In special situations such as k-flagged assassins who god follow, 
       assassin rules and regulations supercede that of the god following 
       rules
** All of these rules assume that the general pkill rules have already been
   taken into account.  See 'help pkill' for general pkill rules.

  (-) Back



